1. DAY-SHIFT 22.8 GB THEN 39 MB vs LIVE SPRINT / B8
========================================================================

## What the 02:14 residual file claimed

`openOODA/audit/f26_residual.oot`:

    Status: p7 hang closed. ... 22.8 GB → 39 MB after agy landed 2c090b8 ...
    What is true today (2026-08-13 02:14 HST)
      oodac check oodac/main.oo direct | 1–2s | 39 MB | 0 | OK
    What was true at 02:00
      oodac check oodac/main.oo ... | 37.66s | 22.8 GB | 1 | ERR type at 159:27
    The 39 MB RSS is the new floor
    Status: Closed-with-day-shift (was 22.8 GB / 32s / rc=1; now 39 MB / 1s / rc=0).

`openOODA/audit/f26_phalanx_rollup.oot` (first wave, same day):

    Memory residual | YES | 22.8 GB RSS peak, 32s wall, linear 699 MiB/s, unbounded
    Fresh /tmp/oodac_new reproduces 22.8 GB

22.8 GB happened. That measurement is not in dispute.

## What live SPRINT / B8 say now

`openOODA/SPRINT.oot` Pin:

    F26 check hang is closed. Live state: 28 seconds, 12 GB RSS (B8 patch);
    1-2 s / 39 MB baseline not recovered (was a different ELF state).

`openOODA/SPRINT.oot` B8 CLOSED:

    Honest delta: 50s / 30 GB -> 28.5s / 12 GB.
    Original 1-2s / 39 MB baseline not recovered.

`openOODA/audit/b8_root_cause.oot`:

    Residual | MED | 12 GB still > 8 GiB WARN; not at 1-2s / 39 MB baseline
    The patch did NOT restore the 1-2 s / 39 MB baseline that the world had
    at 02:14. That baseline was a different ELF (10e9128a…, 984 888 B);
    the current head is dedee1d8… (878 392 B). The pre-patch F26 baseline
    from the very first wave was 22 239 MiB at 32 s, not 1-2 s / 39 MB.
    RSS: 12 GB vs 39 MB baseline. Still 308× larger. NOT recovered.

